A||N||6||reddog||Schrader valve||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||11-22-2001||05:29 PM||||Does anyone know how to remove the valve stem from the schrader valve. I bought a Fuel pressure gauge kit from the Fiero Store and it said to remove the valve stem from the valve to mount the Guage. Anyone done this before? Happy Thanksgiving!!!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thanksgiving_card_small.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by reddog (edited 11-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||jimmybpei||11-22-2001||05:38 PM||||i do believe you need a tire valve stem remover.<P>Later <BR>Jimmy B.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||11-22-2001||05:58 PM||||You can use a tire valve core remover if you just happen to have one, but most people don't carry one around (including myself).<P>I use a small pick.  If you have a skinny pick, or anything hard and small for that matter, that will fit into the small slot on both sides of the valve core, you can use it to turn the core out.  Just stick it in one slot and twist the core; it may be kinda tough to start, but it'll come.  Oh, also press down on the valve before you start to make sure there's no pressure in the line.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||reddog||11-22-2001||06:21 PM||||Thanks guys I'm going to be pulling the intake and throttle body off tommorrow and putting on a Bored out Throttle body and upper plenum that I sent off to Darrel Morse.Also while I have the intake off I bought some Tomco injectors an adjustable Fuel pressure regulator and the pressure gauge I was asking about. I have to get this all done before Monday because I am having a freind replace the timing chain and sprockets as well as putting a power pulley on.Then its off to Georgia on the 10th to put in the NX nitrous system that I am buying from Trav (1fst2m6).Now I just have to find someone to install the shift kit that I bought from the Fiero Store!! Anyone close by that could help??<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ka4nkf||11-22-2001||08:52 PM||||You can buy some metal valve caps at any auto store, or Wal-mart-, K-mart and so on.<BR>one end of these caps is slotted to get the valve core out. try any tire store they will probably give you one.||||reg||1
Z||000005||avengador1||11-22-2001||09:38 PM||||You can usually find them in the bicycle section of your local Walmart. Look for them near the tire patch kits.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||11-23-2001||04:39 AM||||Ooooooor, you can just use a miniature screwdriver, or a pick, or a small drill bit, or a thick paperclip, etc.  Guys, save a buck or however long it takes to get one and be creative..lol..it's just a schrader valve, doesn't take anything special if you're just doing it a few times.  Silly people out there... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
